                "692765c2ed9f1dc2e9123a268212b9a981457e7b"
            ],
            "ref": "refs/changes/14/81614/7",
            "uploader": {
                "name": "Derek Howard",
                "email": "derekh@us.ibm.com",
                "username": "derekhoward55"
            },
            "createdOn": 1751553422,
            "author": {
                "name": "Derek Howard",
                "email": "derekh@us.ibm.com",
                "username": "derekhoward55"
            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "designs/multi-chassis-power.md",
                    "line": 85,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Considering this is your proposal and essentially nobody uses phosphor-power except for IBM, you're not likely to get very much useful feedback on this.  You've essentially created an IBM-only \"playground\" in phosphor-power now."
                },
                {
                    "file": "designs/multi-chassis-power.md",
                    "line": 92,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Shawn McCarney",
                        "email": "shawnmm@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "smccarney"
                    },
                    "message": "In the last few years there has been a shift to move system-specific configuration files into the same repo that contains the code (such as EM).  Would it make sense to put the JSON file in a subdirectory within phosphor-power?  That is where the other JSON files are for the phosphor-power apps."
                },
                {
                    "file": "designs/multi-chassis-power.md",
                    "line": 130,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Shawn McCarney",
                        "email": "shawnmm@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "smccarney"
                    },
                    "message": "In the phosphor-power repository, the current service files are named to match the application, such as `phosphor-regulators.service`.  It is not a hard requirement, but it would be more consistent to name it `phosphor-chassis-power.service`."
                },
                {
                    "file": "designs/multi-chassis-power.md",
                    "line": 152,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "This is a pretty non-useful statement.  What is interesting is what repositories _are_ going to be affected in order to support your new feature.  I assume this is going to have impact to other repositories, so you need to enumerate them."
                },
                {
                    "file": "designs/multi-chassis-power.md",
                    "line": 168,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Shawn McCarney",
                        "email": "shawnmm@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "smccarney"
                    },
                    "message": "From the discussion earlier in this document, maybe tests like the following would be good too?\n* Test where some chassis are removed (not present)\n* Test where power cable is removed from all PSUs\n* Test where cabling / hardware that connects the BMC to a non-BMC chassis is not working (if relevant given hardware design)."
                }
            ],
